  "title": "Liu Bei Rescues Kong Rong at Beihai; Lü Bu Defeats Cao Cao at Puyang",
  "year": "193-194",
  "summary": [
    "Kong Rong, besieged in Beihai by rebels, is broken out by a single rider — Taishi Ci, repaying a kindness done to his mother — and then sends to Liu Bei for help. Liu Bei's reaction to being asked is the most revealing line he has: 'Does Kong Rong know there is a Liu Bei in the world?'",
    "He goes on to Xuzhou to lift Cao Cao's siege, and finds it lifted for him: Lü Bu, prompted by Chen Gong, has taken Yan province while Cao Cao's back was turned, and Cao Cao must go home."
  ],
  "history": "Historical in outline. The novel gives Liu Bei the rescue of both Beihai and Xuzhou; the record is thinner and less flattering to everyone.",
